<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <style type="text/css">
    .main {
      font-family: "Lucida Grande", "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      color: #333;
      font-size: 14px;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 100px auto 0px auto;
      background-image: url('<%= @doubtfire_host %>/assets/images/logo.png');
      background-size: 3.5em;
      background-repeat: no-repeat;
      background-position: top 40px right 45px;
      padding: 30px 40px;
      border: solid 1px rgb(240, 240, 240);
      line-height: 200%;
      text-align: justify;
    }
    footer, .footer {
      font-family: "Lucida Grande", "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: 10px;
      color: #aaa;
      font-size: 0.7em;
    }
    .subtext {
      color: #aaa;
      font-size: 0.7em;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      margin-top: -10px;
    }
    a, a:visited {
      color: #6a97d2;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
    ul {
      list-style: none;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 1.1em;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="main">
    <h1><%= @unit.name %> - Daily LMS Sync Turned Off</h1>
    <p class="subtext"><%= @unit.code %></p>

    <p>Hi <%= @convenor.first_name %>,</p>

    <% if @failing_since %>
    <p>
      The daily LMS <%= @sync_name %> for <%= @unit.code %> has failed every night since
      <strong><%= @failing_since.strftime('%A %-d %B') %></strong>, so <%= @doubtfire_product_name %> has stopped syncing the unit with the LMS.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is usually an outage of the LMS or of <%= @doubtfire_product_name %>'s LMS connection rather than a problem with the unit's settings.
      The last error was: <em><%= @error_message %></em>
    </p>
    <% else %>
    <p>
      The daily LMS <%= @sync_name %> for <%= @unit.code %> failed, so <%= @doubtfire_product_name %> has stopped syncing the unit with the LMS until you review it.
    </p>
    <% if @issues.any? %>
    <p>
      The LMS integration no longer matches the LMS course:
      <ul>
        <% @issues.each do |issue| %>
        <li>
          <% if issue[:lms_group_name].present? %><strong><%= issue[:lms_group_name] %>:</strong><% end %>
          <%= issue[:message] %>
        </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <% else %>
    <p>The error was: <em><%= @error_message %></em></p>
    <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <p>
      These settings have been turned off:
      <ul>
        <% @turned_off.each do |setting| %>
        <li><strong><%= setting %></strong></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </p>

    <% if @failing_since %>
    <p>
      Once the LMS is working again, run a preview import to check what will change, then turn these settings back on in the
      <a href="<%= @lms_url %>">unit's LMS tab</a>.
    </p>
    <% else %>
    <p>Fix the integration in the <a href="<%= @lms_url %>">unit's LMS tab</a>, then turn these settings back on.</p>
    <% end %>

    <p>
      Cheers, <br />
      The <%= @doubtfire_product_name %> Team
    </p>
  </div>
  <footer class="footer">
    Generated with <%= @doubtfire_product_name %>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
